{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevGz9nY1ugTiUFcC2u19","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- `ShipmentController.kt:26-43` — `POST /shipments` creates shipments in CREATED status\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:15-27` — save/findById/existsById methods for persistence\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:19-24` — ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404) patterns\n- `ErrorCode.kt:31-37` — enum with existing SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND and SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS codes\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28` — centralized error conversion to ApiError envelope\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt:42-83` — existing tests using MockMvc and jsonPath assertions\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Controllers inject repository and throw ApiException subclasses for errors\n2. 201 Created for successful POST create; 200 OK for state-changing operations\n3. ConflictException → 409 status; ResourceNotFoundException → 404 status\n4. GlobalExceptionHandler converts all ApiException to ApiError JSON envelope automatically\n5. ErrorCode enum drives error responses; clients switch on codes\n6. Tests use MockMvc, jsonPath assertions, @BeforeEach to reset repository\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ErrorCode.kt` — add SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE for 409 response when confirming CANCELLED shipment\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — add POST /{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — add tests for all four confirm cases (CREATED→CONFIRMED, idempotent, CANCELLED rejection, 404)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Breaking existing tests if endpoint handling is incorrect\n- Not implementing idempotency correctly (retry safety)\n- Using wrong HTTP status codes for the cases\n- Missing error code causes generic error response instead of specific code\n\n**Open questions:** None identified; requirements are fully specified.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ErrorCode.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the enum. This represents when a shipment exists but is in an invalid state for the operation (e.g., CANCELLED).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new endpoint method:\n   ```kotlin\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): ResponseEntity<Shipment>\n   ```\n   Logic:\n   - Fetch shipment or throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND)\n   - If status is CREATED: update to CONFIRMED and save\n   - If status is CONFIRMED: do nothing (idempotent, return current state)\n   - If status is CANCELLED: throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE)\n   - Return 200 OK with the shipment\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four test cases:\n   - `confirms a created shipment to CONFIRMED status` — create S-1, POST confirm, verify status is CONFIRMED\n   - `idempotent confirm succeeds on already confirmed shipment` — confirm twice, both succeed\n   - `confirm rejects a cancelled shipment with 409` — create, manually set to CANCELLED in repo, POST confirm, expect 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n   - `confirm rejects unknown shipment with 404` — POST confirm on non-existent id, expect 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Using existing error codes without adding SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE: Rejected because the ticket requires error responses to be \"consistent with the rest of this API\", and this API uses specific ErrorCode values for each error case. SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE is semantically different from SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS and deserves its own code.\n- POST with a RequestBody containing new status: Rejected because a confirm operation is idempotent and should not require a body; following REST conventions where state transitions are named endpoints (like /confirm).\n- Returning 201 Created on confirm: Rejected because 201 is for resource creation; 200 OK is correct for state-change operations on existing resources.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Processing | Output | HTTP Status |\n|------|-------|-----------|--------|------------|\n| CREATED→CONFIRMED | shipmentId | GET, status==CREATED? Yes → update to CONFIRMED, save | Shipment with CONFIRMED status | 200 OK |\n| Idempotent retry | shipmentId | GET, status==CONFIRMED? Yes → skip update, return current | Same shipment unchanged | 200 OK |\n| CANCELLED reject | shipmentId | GET, status==CANCELLED? Yes → throw ConflictException | ApiError envelope with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE | 409 Conflict |\n| Not found | shipmentId | GET returns null → throw ResourceNotFoundException | ApiError envelope with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND | 404 Not Found |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n| Test | Case | Coverage |\n|------|------|----------|\n| `confirms_created_shipment` | CREATED→CONFIRMED | Endpoint exists, status changes, returns 200 with updated shipment |\n| `confirm_idempotent_on_already_confirmed` | Retry safety | Calling confirm twice succeeds both times, no error |\n| `confirm_rejects_cancelled_shipment` | Invalid state | 409 status, error code is SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE |\n| `confirm_rejects_unknown_shipment` | Not found | 404 status, error code is SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1326,"cache_read_input_tokens":15457,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1326},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4933461b-8637-4fa4-a387-38e1aa5e566d","uuid":"3205178f-c86a-4948-836a-c1601a5840ff","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:02:20.675Z","request_id":"req_011CevGz98qW7QeGyyVq69Zb"}
